<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX5-QA1-017>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX5-QA1-017" ;
  triage:title "ReadDeadline::new(HERDR_REQUEST_DEADLINE).expect() is reachable from the production tick path" ;
  triage:description "AX.5 QA-1 (quality-mgr ax5-qa-r1, PR #1201 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T12:38Z) at head da823baaa0018933f8daac388733c51eb14e9335. rust-qa-agent QA-003: crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs:412 calls ReadDeadline::new(HERDR_REQUEST_DEADLINE).expect(...) on the production tick path; it is safe today only because the constant is fixed-positive, and a future edit to zero would panic at runtime instead of failing to compile. Fix: construct the deadline once (const/OnceLock validated at startup with a compile-time or startup assertion) or handle the Err by skipping the step with a warn." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
